.TH TENSOR-GPU-RESTORE-MAILBOX 1 "2026-11-25" "Tensor Ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
 tensor-gpu-restore-mailbox \- private one-consumer GPU wallpaper restoration handoff
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tensor-gpu-restore-mailbox.py
.RI [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a source-only Python library, not an executable restoration command.
It atomically publishes a 32-character lowercase hexadecimal restoration
grant in the caller-owned (0700) GPU lease-state directory as a 0600 file.
The Wallpaper Engine systemd entrypoint consumes the pending file once and
passes the value in-process to the existing guarded arbiter. The arbiter must
verify the token against SQLite while holding gpu-lease.lock. The transport
file alone never authorizes GPU work or service startup.
.SH SECURITY
The token is never passed through process arguments or environment variables,
and the library does not print it. Only the existing single-user trust boundary
is enforced: other programs running as the same user can access the private
lease database. The caller must serialize restoration attempts using the
existing gpu-restore.lock. An unsuccessful systemd start must revoke any
unconsumed grant. Source-only tests do not prove production readiness.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Display usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tensor-gpu-lease (1),
.BR tensor-gpu-wallpaper-arbiter (1),
.BR tensor-gpu-wallpaper-systemd (1)
